        "Solution (S) Sub-parameters": "S1: The agent provides accurate and complete solutions relevant to the customer’s reported issue.",
        "Solution (S) Observations": "Comment: S1: The agent provided an inaccurate or incomplete solution that did not address the user’s concern.\r\n\r\nUpon further review, no expedite action or Expedite Delivery Request (EDR) was filed despite the order meeting the criteria for a stuck or no-movement parcel concern.\r\n\r\nFor reference: kb-client/article/95893\r\nNo Movement / Stuck Order SOP\r\nCheck if the order qualifies for EDR. \r\n(No movement 3 or more days) since 05-14-2026 09:00 +0800\r\nFile an Expedite Delivery Request (EDR) or follow up on an existing one following the steps in the Expedite Delivery Process\r\n\r\nSuggestion for further success:\r\nAs a best practice, thoroughly review the applicable solution guidelines in KB when handling delayed or stuck orders to ensure all required resolution steps are completed. When an order qualifies for EDR due to prolonged inactivity, proceed with filing or following up on the Expedite Delivery Request and communicate the action clearly to the customer.\r\n\r\nApplying aligned resolutions helps improve handling accuracy, customer expectation setting, and overall case management consistency.",
