        "Greeting & Etiquette (GE)": "No",
        "Greeting & Etiquette (GE) Sub-parameters": "GE4: The agent asked for additional time if more than two minutes were needed to place the user on hold.",
        "Greeting & Etiquette (GE) Observations": "Comment: GE4: The agent did not request additional time when the hold exceeded 2 minutes.\r\nAn opportunity was observed to provide timely hold updates and request additional time when the interaction exceeded the required 2-minute response threshold. During the interaction, the customer experienced an extended wait time without a follow-up update or request for additional time.\r\n\r\nObserved Timeline:\r\n14:43:33 to 14:47:35 :Total hold time recorded was 4 minutes and 2 seconds\r\n\r\nSuggestion for further success:\r\nAs a best practice, provide proactive holding statements before the 2-minute threshold is reached and request additional time whenever further checking or processing is required. This helps maintain customer engagement, manages expectations effectively, and reassures the customer that the concern is still being actively handled.\r\n\r\nSample Statements:\r\n“Thank you for patiently waiting while I continue reviewing your concern.”\r\n“May I ask for an additional 1–2 minutes while I further check the details for you?”\r\nConsistent communication during extended hold times can help improve customer experience and adherence to response time expectations.",
        "Effective Communication (EC)": "Yes",
