        "Effective Communication (EC) Observations": "Comment: EC4: The agent used long or confusing sentences that caused misunderstanding (more than 3 sentences per reply). (Did not follow Long Message SOP)\r\nAn opportunity was observed to follow the Long Message SOP by ensuring clarity, structure, and readability of updates provided to the customer. Upon further review, at chat time stamp *02 June, 09:38:16*, multiple order updates were combined into a single long message containing several tracking statuses and dates across different orders, which may make it difficult for the customer to quickly identify the status of each parcel.\r\n\r\nSuggestion for Further Success:\r\nAs a best practice, ensure that order updates are broken down into separate, clearly labeled messages per order or per tracking update. Instead of combining multiple tracking details in one long paragraph, present each order status individually with its corresponding tracking number and latest update.\r\n\r\nThis approach can help:\r\n\r\n* Improve clarity and readability of multiple order updates\r\n* Make it easier for customers to understand each parcel’s status\r\n* Reduce confusion caused by mixed tracking information",
